ity’s stated worship and reliance into a desired stable manner of proceeding, rather than standing apart from its practice.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"1:5\",\"ar\":\"إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:6\",\"ar\":\"ٱهْدِنَا ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:7\",\"ar\":\"صِرَٰطَ ٱلَّذِينَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The same plural community moves from present declarations of service and reliance to asking for a path associated with a group of people.\",\"limits\":\"The verses do not explicitly describe repetition or say that the path is a settled habit.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"medium\"}\n{\"id\":\"S-hft-base_embodied_guidance_coactive\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"Worship and the appeal for aid precede the request, which supports human service alongside sought assistance; the claim that worship prepares or levels the road is not shown by this sequence.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"1:5\",\"ar\":\"إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:6\",\"ar\":\"ٱهْدِنَا ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ\"}],\"missing\":\"A Quranic usage showing that نَعْبُدُ here invokes the root’s road-preparation sense, or a textual statement that worshipers prepare this route, could establish the proposed coactive mechanism.\",\"support\":\"weak\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"S-hft-base_sustaining_course_inhabited\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The path is specified through people and their contrasting conditions, so its uprightness can be heard as a course recognized by the kind of life and relation to favor it bears.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"1:6\",\"ar\":\"ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:7\",\"ar\":\"صِرَٰطَ ٱلَّذِينَ أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ غَيْرِ ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا ٱلضَّآلِّينَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The following verse identifies the route through people who received favor and sets them against two excluded groups.\",\"limits\":\"No word here denotes dwelling, softness, or material habitability.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"S-hft-ctx_dynamic_between_failures\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The desired route is framed against two contrasting exclusions: people under anger and people who are astray. The path’s identity thus includes distinction from both outcomes.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"1:6\",\"ar\":\"ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:7\",\"ar\":\"غَيْرِ ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا ٱلضَّآلِّينَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The exclusion particles غَيْرِ and وَلَا attach the two groups to the description of the path.\",\"limits\":\"This contrast does not itself establish images of rigidity, disappearance, or continued motion between them.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"S-hft-outlier_restored_sight\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"The contrast between a requested way and those who are astray permits an orientation analogy, but the surah contains no eye or sight language.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"1:5\",\"ar\":\"وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:6\",\"ar\":\"ٱهْدِنَا ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:7\",\"ar\":\"وَلَا ٱلضَّآلِّينَ\"}],\"missing\":\"A Quranic occurrence connecting these roots in these senses to impaired or restored sight, or an explicit visual term in the surrounding passage, could support the ocular reading.\",\"support\":\"weak\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"S-hft-outlier_anti_scattering_collective\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"The petition’s plural object and the people named in 1:7 make a shared course salient, but the text does not say that the group is scattering or that cohesion is at risk.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"1:6\",\"ar\":\"ٱهْدِنَا ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:7\",\"ar\":\"صِرَٰطَ ٱلَّذِينَ\"}],\"missing\":\"A scattering or dispersion term in this passage, or a Quranic parallel linking guidance to preventing a group’s dispersal, could supply the proposed threat to collective unity.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"S-hft-outlier_gift_return_circuit\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The sequence can be heard as relational exchange: the community declares worship and dependence, asks for guidance, and invokes people to whom God has already granted favor as a precedent for guidance received as a gift.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"1:5\",\"ar\":\"إِيَّاكَ نَعْبُدُ وَإِيَّاكَ نَسْتَعِينُ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:6\",\"ar\":\"ٱهْدِنَا ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:7\",\"ar\":\"أَنْعَمْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ\"}],\"activation\":\"The sequence places human service and dependence before the request, then names divine favor as the precedent for the sought route.\",\"limits\":\"The text does not establish that هَدَى means a returned offering here or describe a literal gift circuit.\",\"support\":\"medium\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"S-hft-outlier_incisive_passage\",\"status\":\"reading\",\"finding\":\"The route functions as a discriminating criterion: 1:7 distinguishes it from two excluded groups, giving the request a boundary-setting force.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"1:6\",\"ar\":\"ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:7\",\"ar\":\"غَيْرِ ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا ٱلضَّآلِّينَ\"}],\"activation\":\"The repeated path noun is followed by explicit exclusions that delimit who is associated with it.\",\"limits\":\"The boundary in this wording does not establish a cutting edge or physical passage through resistance.\",\"support\":\"strong\",\"relevance\":\"high\"}\n{\"id\":\"S-hft-outlier_reconstruction_after_collapse\",\"status\":\"open\",\"finding\":\"The request and the exclusion of other groups allow a possible restoration reading, but the surah does not say that the petitioners themselves have suffered collapse or need structural repair.\",\"evidence\":[{\"ref\":\"1:2\",\"ar\":\"رَبِّ ٱلْعَٰلَمِينَ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:6\",\"ar\":\"ٱهْدِنَا ٱلصِّرَٰطَ ٱلْمُسْتَقِيمَ\"},{\"ref\":\"1:7\",\"ar\":\"غَيْرِ ٱلْمَغْضُوبِ عَلَيْهِمْ وَلَا ٱلضَّآلِّينَ\"}],\"missing\":\"